  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Access to Justice and Human Rights at the Sub-National Levels</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Access to Justice and Human Rights at the Sub-national Level Project is to support implementation of new legal aid policy at the sub-national level reaching the most vulnerable population. The objectives of the project is to enhance access to justice through institutional reform in Nepal. The project is to contribute three outputs: 
Output 1: Legal aid authorities and providers effectively manage and provide legal aid services to people, in particular women and other marginalized groups, in a sustainable and quality
Output 2: Justice sector strengthened to provide effective legal/ judicial remedies in line with national and international standards 
Output 3: People, in particular women, Dalit, PWD, LGBTIQ+, poor and other marginalized groups, are empowered to claim their rights and participate in judicial governance/civic life</narrative>
  </description>
